{
  "name": "10-Tenant Overload — 120% Nameplate for 15 min",
  "description": "Stress scenario derived from demo-10-tenant-full-ceiling. All 10 colo tenants run at full contracted ceiling throughout the 3-hour simulation. At t = 30:00 a massive compute burst fires for exactly 15 minutes, driving total site facility draw to 48.3 MW — 120% of the 40.25 MW generation nameplate and beyond what the fleet can sustain. The three gas turbines (hot/warm/cold) and 6 MW / 8 MWh BESS must absorb the step; BESS SoC will deplete rapidly and the reserve-gap alert will fire. At t = 45:00 the burst clears and the site recovers. Use this to observe overload protection, SoC recovery, and generator re-commitment sequencing. (seed=42, deterministic replay.)",
